From 0b900ca7af08a3ad5479a929b7790e4a907be506 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Simin (Simon) Yuan" <yleven120@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:46:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): cut runaway repetition loops mid-stream on
 Bedrock and Codex

Wires the existing RunawayStreamWatch into the Bedrock Converse and Codex Responses streams, so a reply that turns into a repetition loop is cut where it starts instead of streaming to the output limit. Both cuts hand off the same way the other two streams do: the response carries _runaway_repetition, and the length path ends the turn.
